<title>UK: CU shares slip on talk of switch advice.</title>
<headline>CU shares slip on talk of switch advice.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Commercial Union plc slipped on Wednesday amid talk that SBC Warburg had recommended switching from the stock into General Accident plc, traders said.</p>
<p>In early trading CU were down 16-1/2 pence to 656 pence. General Accident shares were 6-1/2 pence higher at 894-1/2 pence.</p>
<p>SBC Warburg analysts declined to comment.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
